{{also|Dunkel}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{term|tunkel|lang=gmh}}, from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|tunkal|lang=goh}}, {{term|tuncal||dark|lang=goh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*dunkalaz||dark}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*dʰengw-||to smoke, fume}}. The voiced onset is first attested in late Middle High German {{term|dunkel|lang=gmh}}; it establishes itself in early modern German through {{etyl|nds-de|de}} influence. Cognates include {{etyl|gml|-}} {{term|dunker||dark|lang=gml}} and Dutch {{term|donker|lang=nl}}.

